WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.920
I'm Taleen Akopyan. I'm
cofounder of Purse Rehab.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.650
We're a family-owned company.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.320
We've been in business for 35 years.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.817
I'm going to walk you
through how my team restores

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:20.700
a $2,000 Louis Vuitton belt bag

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.030
that's been slashed.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.180
It's from their 2003 collection,
so it's discontinued.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.030
Our client reached out to us.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.988
Unfortunately, this was part of

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:32.613
an argument with an ex-boyfriend,

00:00:32.613 --> 00:00:35.754
who decided to slash her favorite bag.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.520
The repair process will
entail several steps.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.830
What we have here is our senior technician

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.360
disassembling the front pocket of the bag

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.330
from the main zipper compartment.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.990
And this is done by undoing the stitching

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.540
that's on the outermost layer.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:59.820
And what we're using here is a round awl

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.300
to open up the stitches.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.160
It's important to use a round awl,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.033
because this will help with
not damaging the canvas.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:13.430
Once we've taken apart the front pocket,

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:16.120
we will move on to the main lining

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:20.320
and we will undo the stitching
there to remove the piping,

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:23.500
which is basically what's
keeping the front pocket

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.750
and the main compartment together.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.367
And, again, we will be using

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:30.366
the same round awl to do this step.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.810
Once we're done with the
deconstruction phase,

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:38.020
we will be replacing the following pieces

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.770
that have the most damage:

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.720
the front pocket, which
includes the lining,

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.678
and the lining that is also

00:01:45.678 --> 00:01:47.745
part of the main compartment,

00:01:47.745 --> 00:01:49.130
which is outer-facing.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.183
So the three layers will be replaced.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.830
Here, we're recreating the pieces

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.690
that we're going to replace.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:03.523
And we do this by making templates

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.464
to match the exact size

00:02:05.464 --> 00:02:08.180
of the original piece
that we're replacing.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:12.290
We're using a sharp knife
to cut out the template.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.500
We have three different
pieces that we'll be doing.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:20.170
So this is an important part
of the replacement process

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.070
to ensure that we get
the exact same template

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.310
that matches the original piece.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:29.960
We are using authentic recycled
Louis Vuitton material.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:33.690
We have the canvas that we'll be replacing

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:36.840
with an authentic piece
that matches the original.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.430
And we are also using the
lining from a recycled bag

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:43.010
that matches the existing lining.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.326
So, in essence, we are using

00:02:45.326 --> 00:02:47.726
the exact same type of material

00:02:47.726 --> 00:02:51.210
to restore the pieces
that we are replacing.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:55.210
Here, our senior technician
is skiving the canvas.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:56.580
Skiving is a process

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.270
where the leather or
canvas is thinned out.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:03.520
It's essentially shaved
to a thinner layer,

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:06.180
and it's typically only
done around the edges

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.640
because those are the areas

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.993
that we're going to fold and stitch.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.900
Once the canvas is skived,

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.180
our technician here is applying glue

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.710
to the area that was skived.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:21.130
And we're using a plastic
container with a pointy tip

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.520
to ensure that the glue is only applied

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.060
to the area that we need to apply to.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.130
We have applied the glue.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:33.220
Now we'll be putting the lining

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:37.500
together with the canvas
that we recreated.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.860
And we apply the heat

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.480
because the heat helps activate the glue

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.147
so that it adheres better and it's secure.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.640
Once we've completed this step,

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.810
we're going to stitch the
Louis Vuitton monogram piece

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:03.160
that we are reusing.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.170
This is the original piece

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:08.940
that we're restitching on
the lining that we cut out.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.080
So the lining is new,

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.810
but the top portion is the existing piece.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:18.160
So, once we restitch this together,

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:23.160
we will bring the front pocket
and the back lining together.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:31.870
Once the two pieces have
been separately stitched,

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.830
we will glue them together
using contact cement glue.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:39.430
We need to glue every piece
before we do the stitching

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:43.680
to ensure there's no movement
and it's very secure.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.810
And once we have the front pocket

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.210
and the back lining together,

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.180
we are going to put in the date code.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.930
This is an important piece

00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:00.920
to retain the authenticity of the bag.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:05.850
Once that's done, the next
step is to reglue the piping

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:09.040
to the trim of the front pocket.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.340
Again, here we're reusing the same piping

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.900
because it wasn't damaged,
and we want to retain

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:18.206
as much of the original parts as possible.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:20.730
After gluing the piping,

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:24.500
we're going to restitch
to the front pocket.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:27.240
You'll notice that the
piping has two stitch lines.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.490
One is to stitch the
piping to the front pocket,

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.373
and the second line is to stitch
it to the main compartment.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.666
The next step here is to patch up

00:05:39.666 --> 00:05:41.849
the interior-lining cut.

00:05:41.849 --> 00:05:44.870
We did not replace the
full interior lining

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.780
in an effort to retain
the original pieces,

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.090
because it wasn't very damaged

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:52.370
and it's a less visible space.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.760
We're using a wider
brush to apply the glue

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.620
because we're working with wider space,

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.133
so we don't have to be as precise.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:12.060
We're now gluing the main compartment

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.380
to the exterior pocket.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:17.900
And we are stapling the
two pieces together.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.030
This is not something

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:21.340
that's typically done in this industry,

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:22.935
but our senior technician

00:06:22.935 --> 00:06:25.350
has been using this
technique for many years.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.050
And it's a successful technique

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:29.920
because it's basically an
added layer of security

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:31.930
to ensure that there's zero movement

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:35.270
when we're stitching
all the pieces together.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.210
And he's hammering down the staples

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:38.680
to ensure that they're flat

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:41.430
and there's no chance of them being caught

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:44.622
in the sewing machine
when we do the stitching.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:48.920
And we're using a guide to ensure

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:52.873
that the stitching is straight
and aligned with the bag.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:59.510
And here we are removing the staples

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:03.190
using a stapler remover,
and this is a rounded tip,

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.963
so it doesn't cause any damage to the bag.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:13.080
We're hammering the edges of the bag

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.500
after turning it right side
out to straighten out the edges

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:19.313
and ensure everything is in place.

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:25.020
Of course, we have to
straighten out the piping

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.360
to make sure everything is in place,

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.943
so that the final stitching

00:07:29.943 --> 00:07:32.984
will be as perfect as possible.

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:39.470
We have to be very careful
in this particular stage

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:43.500
to ensure that the needles
go back into the same holes.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:46.860
So we have to be very
focused and very careful

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.560
in making sure that we are using

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.628
not only the same color thread,

00:07:50.628 --> 00:07:52.970
the thickness of the thread has to match,

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:55.656
and we follow the holes accordingly.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:02.275
I'm super pleased with the results

00:08:02.275 --> 00:08:06.008
and so proud of our team
and our senior technician

00:08:06.008 --> 00:08:07.670
for taking this challenge on

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:10.210
and giving this bag a second life.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:13.119
I can't wait to share it with our client.

